{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"},"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" product to the test target. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" binds a fresh"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker to the test’s task for the length of its body, then returns every event tracked in it, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. Here "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SignedUp"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Testing","import TrackerTesting","","@Test func signingUpTracksThePlan() async {","    let tracked = await withRecordingTracker {","        Tracker.current.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","    }","    #expect(tracked.events(of: SignedUp.self) == [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")])","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each call has a tracker of its own, so tests running at the same time never see each other’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events. The body may be sync or async, and may return a value, read as ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracked.value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracked.names","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists every event’s name and ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracked.records","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" every record.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Code that is handed its tracker rather than reading "},{"code":"Tracker.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", such as a SwiftUI view given"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one with "},{"code":"tracker(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", takes the one the body is given: "},{"code":"withRecordingTracker { tracker in … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews"]}],"references":{"doc://TrackerTesting/documentation/TrackerTesting":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackertesting","role":"collection","title":"TrackerTesting","abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","title":"Traffluent"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","role":"article","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","abstract":[{"text":"Give views the tracker the way each frame